===Etymology===
From earlier {{m|es|culantro}}, from {{etyl|la|es}} {{m|la|coriandrum}} (compare {{cog|fr|coriandre}}, {{cog|it|coriandolo}}, {{cog|pt|coentro}}) from {{etyl|grc|es}} {{m|grc|κορίαννον||coriander}}, {{m|grc|κορίανδρον}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{es-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{es-noun|m}}

# [[coriander]], [[#English|cilantro]]

====Usage notes====
* Unlike the English term borrowed from it, the Spanish term refers to both the plants and the seeds.

